      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is Pred?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pred is a peer-to-peer sports prediction exchange built on Base. Traders match positions through an on-chain order book, with USDC-denominated positions that earn native yield. Settlement is 200ms, market resolution is 3 minutes. Backed by Accel and Coinbase Ventures."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What were Pred's beta metrics?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "In an 8-week private beta, Pred achieved 86% week-over-week retention, 83% repeat deposit rate, and over 100,000 trades across 300+ invited users, generating approximately $5 million in notional volume."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is Pred different from a sportsbook?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Pred is a peer-to-peer exchange — traders set prices against each other, not against a house. Sportsbooks embed a 4–8% vig into every market. Pred charges a transparent exchange fee averaging under 2%, and does not limit winning traders."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What makes the 2026 FIFA World Cup significant for prediction markets?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The 2026 World Cup features 48 teams and 104 matches across the U.S., Canada, and Mexico. Global regulated sportsbook volume is projected at $60 billion, with U.S. prediction market volume projected at over $2.5 billion. Polymarket's World Cup winner contracts had already reached $1.5 billion in traded value before the tournament began."
      }
    }
  ]
